  "limits": [
    "Only two ordered boots per CPU count on an active host; no confidence interval or statistical significance claim.",
    "Warm results overlap between individual boots, and the first two-vCPU boot is substantially slower than the second; pooled percentages are descriptive.",
    "Cold means first browser launch after a fresh guest boot; host APFS caches were not purged and may remain warm.",
    "The workload measures headless startup, local JS/layout and PNG encoding, not UTM GUI responsiveness, desktop frame rate, Tor throughput or native application parity.",
    "Host CPU spans sampled boot, settling and benchmark time. Host RSS is sampled, not an exact peak or guest RAM demand.",
    "Host swap/page counters include other applications. All trials experienced host-wide swapping; it cannot be attributed to the benchmark guests.",
    "Guest available RAM is sampled at 0.25-second intervals; short-lived peaks can be missed. This small workload does not establish memory needs for sustained browsing.",
    "Guests have zero SwapTotal, so zero guest swap counters do not demonstrate swap-backed safety. Launch-window OOM, reclaim and memory-pressure deltas were zero; this small workload does not justify reducing RAM."
